Genesis 1.2.1 (genesis-world wheel) CPU rigid-solver patch for TopoGym's articulated fiber bundle; applied by
images/topogym/Dockerfile with sha256 checks of both files before and after (patch -p1 in the genesis package dir).
1. abd/forward_dynamics.py: on the CPU backend without hibernation the mass matrix is assembled on its structural entries
   (same-link pairs and ancestor links, mirrored) and factored by a tree-sparse LDL^T that walks each pivot's ancestor
   DOFs only (func_factor_mass_tree): the same updates in the same order as the dense CPU branch, so the physical state is
   bit-identical (entries outside the ancestor pattern stay exact zeros instead of being rewritten as x - a*0.0, which
   only flips signs of zeros); other backends / options fall back to func_factor_mass.
2. constraint/solver.py: the skyline DOF permutation keeps Genesis' order except inside entities with more than 64 DOFs,
   whose DOFs are eliminated children-first (fill-free for a tree); robots (15-16 DOFs) and free bodies keep exactly the
   previous permutation, so only the fiber bundle (318 / 558 DOFs) sees a round-off-level change.
Validation: docs/rcb/benchmarks/topogym.md (fiber_bundling CPU speed, 2026-10-05).

